the C20 setting so o want more books! With the other lines closed for the move to 5th ed we still have more here to develop!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T00:24:51-08:00","id":1266892,"title":"","content":"Also I need more Piskies fluff and direction! As is their group nature makes them to egoless and collectivist for me to grock...<br /> <br /> I mean if I want a manic Pixie kith I may need to finish a Sprite kith...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T00:31:03-08:00","id":1266894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1266891#post1266891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really love the C20 setting so o want more books! With the other lines closed for the move to 5th ed we still have more here to develop!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mage and wraith are still open","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T00:51:22-08:00","id":1266897,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, but Changeling is what I\u2019ve been most happy with 20ifying.<br /> <br /> Mage seems self contained for me, well they will add a book for the Digitalweb and Technocracy reloaded but we won\u2019t get Sorcerers and Archmages. So Changeling feels the most alive to me, with the most room to expand!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T12:47:43-08:00","id":1267057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1266897#post1266897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, but Changeling is what I\u2019ve been most happy with 20ifying.<br /> <br /> Mage seems self contained for me, well they will add a book for the Digitalweb and Technocracy reloaded but we won\u2019t get Sorcerers and Archmages. So Changeling feels the most alive to me, with the most room to expand!</div> </div> </div> </div>mage still has Gods and Monsters, Book of the Fallen, Technocracy Reloaded, Digital web 3.0. Victorian age mage. That's the MOST books of any line promised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T18:10:03-08:00","id":1267152,"title":"","content":"As well, Archmages and sorcerers aren't getting much coverage because there's comparatively low demand for them: I for one am far more interested in M20 supplements for the Traditions and Disparates before seeing M20 updates for sorcerers and Archmages: finish covering the basics before you address fringe issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T22:17:09-08:00","id":1267194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1267057#post1267057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> mage still has Gods and Monsters, Book of the Fallen, Technocracy Reloaded, Digital web 3.0. Victorian age mage. That's the MOST books of any line promised.</div> </div> </div> </div>No what I mean is I\u2019m most excited for The Reloaded and Digital Web Book, the gods and Monster and Fallen books may either be great or meh... it depends.<br /> <br /> <br /> And with the nature of Mage I stand by not needing a traditions or Disparates book before Archmages and Sorcerers. I found revised info to be quite sufficient. But the problem is we only have a few people who have the crunch chops to do an Archmage book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T11:53:10-08:00","id":1267370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1267194#post1267194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No what I mean is I\u2019m most excited for The Reloaded and Digital Web Book, the gods and Monster and Fallen books may either be great or meh... it depends.<br /> <br /> <br /> And with the nature of Mage I stand by not needing a traditions or Disparates book before Archmages and Sorcerers. I found revised info to be quite sufficient. But the problem is we only have a few people who have the crunch chops to do an Archmage book...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Counter point on having a Revised Book for Sorcerers and Archmages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T12:36:08-08:00","id":1267386,"title":"","content":"\u2026all of which has very little to do with Kithbooks. Shall we continue this in the Mage forum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T20:31:26-08:00","id":1269423,"title":"","content":"I'm all for more Kithbooks but I'd honestly want to see things like a book of Gallain, a Book going more into the Hsien and their Courts and other Fae of Asian Culture, a Book about the Nunnehi and their Cultures as well as Chimera and Spirit beings that might play big roles in their societies, I'd like to see a Book of Thallain that acted as an updated version of the Shadow Court book, I'd like to see a Book that gave more concrete rules about the Denizens or the Inanimae since it seemed like quite a bit was left out on the cutting room floor regarding both kinds of fae, most Importantly I'd love to see a Victorian Age Fae/Changeling book that showed how the Transition between Dark Ages: Fae and Changeling: the Dreaming could have happened or at least showed a time before the Return of the Shining Host and how the Fae existed during a period when Reason and Folklore still existed hand in hand.<br /> <br /> There's quite a lot of things I'd love to see but I certainly wouldn't say no to Kithbooks or a Lore of the Kiths style book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T01:07:59-08:00","id":1269476,"title":"","content":"I would like a serious well done Clurichaun book that inspects them from origins and other angles. Something that addresses the Leprechaun myth, drawing the ties of the earlier name of Lugherpagne, crippled god Lugh, as them possibly being a degeneration of the Sidhe. Maybe even split Lucherpane and the Clarichaun as two castes or even a social thing or another word for Seelie and Unseelie.<br /> <br /> And I want a Gallainbook all for the Merfolk, fleshing out their history and reintroducing their houses.<br /> <br /> And I feel the Morganed have a niche place among the Kithain even when we have the Merfolk. They are for telling stories of the Sea from thelands point of view and they dwell with the Other Kithain.<br /> <br /> I want something to finally cover Nymphs, maybe make The various types of Nymphs specific Inanimae Phyla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T05:34:11-08:00","id":1269519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jane_Dargason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1269423#post1269423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for more Kithbooks but I'd honestly want to see things like a book of Gallain, a Book going more into the Hsien and their Courts and other Fae of Asian Culture, a Book about the Nunnehi and their Cultures as well as Chimera and Spirit beings that might play big roles in their societies, I'd like to see a Book of Thallain that acted as an updated version of the Shadow Court book, I'd like to see a Book that gave more concrete rules about the Denizens or the Inanimae since it seemed like quite a bit was left out on the cutting room floor regarding both kinds of fae, most Importantly I'd love to see a Victorian Age Fae/Changeling book that showed how the Transition between Dark Ages: Fae and Changeling: the Dreaming could have happened or at least showed a time before the Return of the Shining Host and how the Fae existed during a period when Reason and Folklore still existed hand in hand.<br /> <br /> There's quite a lot of things I'd love to see but I certainly wouldn't say no to Kithbooks or a Lore of the Kiths style book.</div> </div> </div> </div>::takes notes::","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T06:00:19-08:00","id":1269530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jane_Dargason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1269423#post1269423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most Importantly I'd love to see a Victorian Age Fae/Changeling book that showed how the Transition between Dark Ages: Fae and Changeling: the Dreaming could have happened or at least showed a time before the Return of the Shining Host and how the Fae existed during a period when Reason and Folklore still existed hand in hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pssst... Luka <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T06:57:54-08:00","id":1269551,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I seem to recall that the original plans for Changeling's historical setting would have been a couple centuries earlier than that, in the Elizabethan age (late 16th century). The Victorian age strikes me as a little late for the transition from Fae to Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:51:09-08:00","id":1269595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jane_Dargason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1269423#post1269423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a Book of Thallain that acted as an updated version of the Shadow Court book,</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Please give us this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T19:29:11-08:00","id":1269724,"title":"","content":"i want Dragons/Drakes/something as a Kith. A full damned kith. Maybe a full damned &quot;Type&quot; like Dragons are their own Gallain equivalent like Inanimae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T07:05:53-08:00","id":1269808,"title":"","content":"I really don't see dragons working in modern Changeling. Maybe in a Shard (I could see doing something with them and other monsters similar to what Chronicles of Darkness did with Beast: the Primordial, but as a bizarre kind of Gallain); but not in the official setting. <br /> <br /> If I recall correctly, Bygone Bestiary addresses dragons. I could see consulting that book for chimerical creatures in general. As well, I've had a Shard in mind for a while now where changelings rescued some of the last surviving mythological creatures by putting some of them through something to the effect of the Changeling Way \u2014 so every so often in the modern day, you'll have a horse that undergoes a Crysalis and emerges with (chimerical) wings or a horn, for example. It's not too different from how Changeling artifacts have a \u201cmortal seeming\u201d, but extended to animals and not just inanimate objects. But again, that wouldn't be something that I'd expect to see in the official setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T15:52:55-08:00","id":1269917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1269808#post1269808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see dragons working in modern Changeling. Maybe in a Shard (I could see doing something with them and other monsters similar to what Chronicles of Darkness did with Beast: the Primordial, but as a bizarre kind of Gallain); but not in the official setting.<br /> <br /> If I recall correctly, Bygone Bestiary addresses dragons. I could see consulting that book for chimerical creatures in general. As well, I've had a Shard in mind for a while now where changelings rescued some of the last surviving mythological creatures by putting some of them through something to the effect of the Changeling Way \u2014 so every so often in the modern day, you'll have a horse that undergoes a Crysalis and emerges with (chimerical) wings or a horn, for example. It's not too different from how Changeling artifacts have a \u201cmortal seeming\u201d, but extended to animals and not just inanimate objects. But again, that wouldn't be something that I'd expect to see in the official setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of things &quot;Address&quot; dragons. They are Bygones. They are Spirits. They are a werecreature type. I mean looking at Beast PLENTY of Kithain/Gallain would already be Beasts.. Your average Redcap, Unseelie Trolls, Rock Giants, hell Clurichain have the whole &quot;hoard&quot; thing. Dragon Kin were even a thing in the Arcadia card game. So I don't think adding some form of Dragon as humanoids wouldn't be an issue(plus there's plenty of stories of human shape dragons seduce men/women in the world...)<br /> <br /> As for your shard idea.. um its in Kingdom of the WIllows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T00:43:51-08:00","id":1270040,"title":"","content":"Yeah I love the idea of dragons, so I\u2019ll take any I can get. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yeah some Fae creatures did get reborn into dogs and horses, someone used to have a thread on expanding the rules for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T07:32:29-08:00","id":1270353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1263606-other-kithbooks?p=1269724#post1269724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i want Dragons/Drakes/something as a Kith. A full damned kith. Maybe a full damned &amp;quot;Type&amp;quot; like Dragons are their own Gallain equivalent like Inanimae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did share my writeup for the Drake kith at one point. Their writeup isn\u2019t canon, but their existence is as much canon as anything else in the C20 Anthology. Provided you trust the narrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>